  "sources": [
    {
      "kind": "datasheet",
      "url": "https://www.aeta-audio.com/downloads/doc/product_data/Scoop5S-IP_ENG.pdf",
      "note": "AETA Scoop5S-IP datasheet 12/2020 (opened, text read): 1U 19'' (WxHxD) 480 x 44 x 252 mm, 3.2 kg, AC 85-263 V, XLR sockets (2 female in, 2 male out analog; 1 female in, 1 male out AES/EBU), Ethernet 100/10BaseT. The S-IP is the IP-only variant of the same chassis."
    },
    {
      "kind": "manual",
      "url": "https://www.aeta-audio.com/downloads/doc/manuals/manual_scoop5S.pdf",
      "note": "AETA Scoop5 S user manual (opened, text read): section 3.2.2 all connections are on the rear panel (IEC mains socket, analog inputs female XLR, outputs male XLR, Ethernet RJ45); section 3.2.1 on/off key at the far left of the front panel, top left corner, hold 3 s (the unit has no mains rocker, it starts as soon as power is applied); section 6.5 says 1U 44 mm and 265 mm overall depth (inconsistent with its own 12.5 inch, so the 252 mm of the datasheet is used)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.aeta-audio.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Scoop5S_2-1.png",
      "note": "AETA rear photo (opened as image, 800x621, near straight-on). Calibrated 1.59 px/mm: plate height 70 px = 44 mm, giving a plate width of 444 mm (706 px); plate assumed centred in the 480 mm box (18 mm offset). The IEC inlet then measures 29 mm wide, consistent with a C14. in-send = ANALOG input A (female XLR, second of the left pair, label A); out-return = analog output A (male XLR, label A). Positions +/- 4 mm. ip = the RJ45 labelled Ethernet. power-in = IEC inlet at the right end."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.aeta-audio.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Scoop5S_1-1.png",
      "note": "AETA front photo (opened as image, 800x621, three-quarter view, so only a rough position). Opposite face = front. power = the round on/off key at the top-left of the front panel, about 10 mm diameter; read 15 mm from the faceplate left edge plus an assumed 17.5 mm rack ear, 30.6 mm from the bottom (+/- 6 mm). Protrusion d = 3 mm is an estimate."
    },
    {
      "kind": "photo",
      "url": "https://www.aeta-audio.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Scoop5S_2-1.png",
      "note": "Wave 5 re-measure of the XLR rows on rear_padded.png (the picture the ports sit on, 1.587 px/mm across and 1.477 px/mm up, read on an 8x grid): INPUT A female XLR centre y 18.7 mm (was 23.9, 5.2 mm above the connector), OUTPUT A male XLR y 20.0 (was 22.6); x unchanged (65.4 and 116.7 agree within 0.1 mm). +/- 0.5 mm."
    }
  ],
